WEBVTT

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.630
I don't regret anything at all! I can't!

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.800
Because...

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:13.640
...what I did was definitely not wrong!

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:37.950
<i>It's strange.</i>

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:40.830
<i>Even after...</i>

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:44.330
<i>so much time has passed,</i>

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:50.840
<i>something can save you,</i>

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.590
<i>coming in like a storm
from a completely different direction.</i>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:01.470
Hina...

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:10.150
Thank you.

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:13.110
You are...

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.240
my lifesaver.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:17.660
I promise.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.620
I'll stay with you.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.410
Rei...

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:31.840
Even if it takes the rest of my life,
I will pay you back.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:07.980
Small World

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:13.400
<i>Sniff-sniff.</i>

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.030
<i>Sniff-sniff.</i>

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.570
Here's dessert!

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:26.660
It's the cherries that Kiriyama brought over.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.710
Cherries!

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.300
Thank you, Kiriyama.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:51.230
NOM NOM

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.230
Delicious!

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.860
<i>They smell sour-meow.</i>

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.980
<i>I'm not crazy about fruit.</i>

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.370
Huh? Are you sleepy, Momo?

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:14.000
Maybe we should take a bath.
Although it's a bit early...

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:23.260
So, Hina, do you want to try playing? Shogi.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.390
SHAKE
SHAKE
SHAKE

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.390
W-Will you go easy on me?

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:35.900
SHAKE
SHAKE
SHAKE

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:35.900
Yes, yes, of course!

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.690
Then would you take it upstairs?

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:41.990
I wanna play some more...

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.240
I'm going to give Momo her bath.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:47.780
*Kawamoto House's
bath changing room
is the living room.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.780
I wanna play with Rei.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:54.870
Kiriyama.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.590
Are you sure that's all you need?

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:01.920
HINA

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:01.920
KIRIYAMA

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.090
Yeah.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:01.380
Are you positive? Just this much?

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:02.300
Yeah.

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:03.510
All right!

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:07.050
Apparently the first time in Hina's room...

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.430
Then I might be able to win!

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.890
- Then let's get started.
- Okay.

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:12.770
Why aren't I going first?

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:14.690
I thought you were going easy on me.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:19.900
There's a rule that with handicap shogi,
the player who's short of pieces goes first.

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:26.030
What? Oh, but... okay. Go ahead.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.030
FIVE MINUTES LATER

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:32.250
I-I lost.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.160
GLOOM

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:36.710
One more! One more time!

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:43.050
Hey, yo, pineapple, lalala,
a strange magical fruit...

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:40.550
I know! I'll just play with two pieces,
the king and a gold general!

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:46.470
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.800
<i>Why am I so bad at this?</i>

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:55.520
Oh. You're taking my Pawn at 5-5?

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:56.940
Good one.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:01.400
<i>If anything, the chairman is skilled at making
his opponents look good and enjoy themselves.</i>

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:04.940
Okay, here's a hint.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.150
With strong pieces, you...

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:07.950
B-Back off and then strike!

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.280
Correct.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:13.910
<i>Mr. Yokomizo takes the time to amuse
and teach even oddball players. It's great.</i>

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:16.160
It's about communication, Kiriyama.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:20.840
Imagine what your opponent is thinking
and what they want to do.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.840
Then get close to their feelings.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:29.590
In the waiting room
of his first shogi event

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:25.840
Look at your opponent closely.

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:28.970
Well, calm down, and let's take it easy.

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:35.230
<i>Look at your opponent closely.</i>

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:38.230
<i>Okay.</i>

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.860
STARE

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.110
Thanks, Rei.

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:50.990
I think I'm starting to get the hang of it,
so I should be okay for the next one.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:55.870
I'm no match for her!
This middle school student is consoling me again!

00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:59.210
Okay, one more time.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:03.380
<i>What's the point of coming here to console her
if she's the one consoling you, Rei Kiriyama?</i>

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:10.140
<i>And suddenly I felt a lump in my throat.</i>

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:14.390
<i>Over the years, how often has this girl smiled</i>

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:17.730
<i>and been considerate
of other people's feelings like this?</i>

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:24.650
Hina.

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:27.110
Listen...

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:33.660
Will you tell me?

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:38.160
A little bit at a time is fine.
About what's happening at school...

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:50.180
Right now, I guess this is what it's like.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:53.050
Like everyone is looking from afar.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:59.430
<i>Hina thought and thought,
slowly sharing bits and pieces with me.</i>

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:03.610
Our groups are set up by order of name,

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:08.610
but at lunch, I can tell
that everyone gets so stiff.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.700
They hardly ever look at me.

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:16.620
It's like only my group is at a wake.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:25.500
And then the silence is suddenly broken by
the loud laughter of the girls who bullied Chiho.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:30.920
Their loud, loud voices...

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:32.970
Their laughter...

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:39.720
It's like there's an invisible hierarchy
within our class.

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:47.020
And your ranking decides
how loud you can laugh

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:53.450
or how much freedom
you're allowed in the classroom.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:58.950
<i>That's the atmosphere of Hina's class.</i>

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:07.040
<i>I'm sure this is a story that everyone
has experienced at one time or another.</i>

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:14.760
There shouldn't even be such a thing.

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:18.430
But... But there is.

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:22.020
It's been there all the time.
Ever since elementary school...

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:31.570
Hey, Kiriyama, what is that?

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:33.320
That atmosphere...

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:38.160
Who's cool? Who's not cool?

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:42.700
When and how is that decided?

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:44.620
Who decides it?

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:50.800
Even though we're all just
the same middle school students.

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:56.930
Even though we're all just
the same human beings.

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:13.320
SILENCE

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:13.030
DISTANCE

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:17.570
Is that what she really said?
What a loser!

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:17.570
CACKLE CACKLE HAHAHA

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:19.570
CACKLE CACKLE CACKLE

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:18.700
CHEW CHEW

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:21.830
CHEW CHEW
MUNCH MUNCH

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:21.830
I'm-telling-you

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:23.080
- Isn't that nuts?
- Totally!

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:25.080
Thank you for the meal.

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:31.130
That's hilarious!

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:33.960
GLOOMY

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.960
<i>Th-This feels so awkward.</i>

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:36.760
Is Kawamoto here?

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:38.390
T-Takahashi?

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:47.850
STING STING STING

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:47.850
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:50.770
No way. I totally tossed that lightly.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:58.450
I heard from Kiriyama.

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:04.200
At lunch time...

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.830
if things get difficult, let's just play catch.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:10.540
If you want more people,
I could call my baseball team buddies to join in.

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:12.090
They're already staring.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.500
A girl!

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.590
Damn you, Takahashi!
This is outrageous!

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:24.720
Kiriyama came over to my house yesterday
to coach us while playing.

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:29.190
Oh, I see. Now I've got it.

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:31.150
For the Silver at 4-3, you go with Pawn at 3-4.

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:35.480
Professional shogi players are so amazing.

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:37.320
That's why you're a professional.

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:40.450
Yeah. I see.

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.490
Well, it's a surprise tactic.

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:45.370
Dad and Grandpa were delighted.

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:49.250
Grandpa's been staying in bed recently,
but he was up and about for this.

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:56.840
Invite me over again for curry.
With the fried chicken.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:00.840
Last time Dad and Grandpa were hogging
Kiriyama, so I couldn't really to talk to him.

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:03.430
Sure.

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:07.890
That hurts!

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:11.480
That can't hurt.

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:11.980
Small World

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:15.980
Letter

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:21.650
Thank you.

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.210
Oh, thank you.

00:12:31.210 --> 00:12:33.250
Good game, Kiriyama 5th-Dan.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:34.710
Thank you.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:53.980
CLENCH

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:54.770
That's four wins!

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:55.650
Yes!

00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:58.780
Just one more win and I'll be
in the Kishousen preliminary semifinals!

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.950
Things are looking up this month!

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:10.540
At the moment, I've got two consecutive wins
for rank-deciding matches.

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:15.790
I'm still in the running for Kishousen,
the Lion King Tournament,

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:17.540
and the Newcomer Tournament.

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:22.670
I'd like to win the Lion King Tournament.

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:26.430
If I can win in group five
and participate in the challenger tournament...

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:31.680
...then I'll hit my financial target!

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:35.230
But with the Newcomer Tournament,
prize money aside,

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:39.400
I want to win one more match,
get to the finals, and build up momentum.

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:52.750
All right, I need to practice.
I'm not going to lose!

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:58.340
I will become the Newcomer King!

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:05.720
Good morning.

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:06.970
Good morning!

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:16.850
STOP FLIRTING AROUND, MORON

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:45.800
<i>I couldn't finish eating everything.</i>

00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:49.640
<i>Is this what they call a stomach ache?</i>

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:58.480
Why didn't you show up?

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:00.650
T-Takahashi!

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:03.690
Bitch.

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:14.740
Um, thanks, Takahashi.

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:17.500
But today, I...

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:21.040
Uh, I think we were
in the same class first year.

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:24.050
Hey, Takagi. That's you, right?

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:35.600
You want to play catch too?

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:40.060
Here I go! You ready?

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:44.360
You go first, Megu!

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.110
No way! I'm scared!

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:48.320
It'll be fine! Go on!

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:49.820
Here I go!

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:53.370
One-two...

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:02.000
Jerk! You suck!

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.290
I'm out of here! That guy's insane!

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:06.130
Megu, wait!

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:09.130
Huh? What, you're leaving already?

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.890
Hey, what's wrong?

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:14.100
Takahashi...

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:15.890
Y-Yikes.

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:18.810
Takahashi.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:22.060
They tossed my glove on the ground
and ran off.

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:28.570
The one who changed schools
was Chiho Sakura, right?

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:33.240
During the overnight field trip in second year,

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:38.870
the wind blew my bento box over
and sand got all over my food.

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:44.130
Then she gave me half of her bento.

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:48.090
She smiled and said, "Here."

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:52.090
At the time, I thought that anyone who
shared their own food was a good person.

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:58.010
So let's play catch anytime.

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:05.810
I kind of feel like it's a good idea
to show them that there are allies too.

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:15.620
I see.

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:18.490
But... I'm sorry.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:21.250
Takahashi is so handsome, huh?

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:24.000
I get it. Now they're envious.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:27.380
I'm so sorry.
I didn't think that far ahead.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:29.340
<i>There are bad people-meow.</i>

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:31.130
<i>No good-meow.</i>

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:32.840
<i>Yeah. Bad-meow.</i>

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:36.470
No, Kiriyama! Don't take it like that!

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:38.390
I'm going to keep playing catch.

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:40.890
After all, it's fun.

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:45.230
And Takahashi seems to remember Chiho.

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:49.520
So I can talk about her,
and that makes me really happy.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:59.240
Nobody talks about Chiho in class anymore,

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:03.580
so it's like she was never there
from the beginning.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:06.790
One person has gone away.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:09.750
So why?

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:15.970
Huh? Sorry.

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:17.890
Here. Take this.

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:26.390
Rei, thank you for always listening to me.

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:33.280
You're always asking me what I want to do.

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:36.910
MIDDLE SCHOOL

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:39.620
But I...

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:49.130
I don't know what I want to do...

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:52.250
...so it's frustrating!

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:02.470
What do I want to do?

00:19:03.970 --> 00:19:07.190
I want to yell "Idiots!" and punch them!

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:11.190
I want to beat the crap out of them!
I want to do to them what they did to Chiho!

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:21.200
And then I want them to realize what they did!

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:18.570
3-2 SAKURA

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:28.710
But it's too late.

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:31.920
Chiho's already gone!

00:19:35.010 --> 00:19:37.220
<i>She sent Chiho a letter,</i>

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:40.050
<i>but never got a response.</i>

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:42.680
<i>Instead, she received a response</i>

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:47.100
Chiho hasn't got back to school, even here.
Right now she's in rehab with a counselor
at a place called "Heart Care Center."
Chiho would like to write to you, but...

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:46.060
<i>from Chiho's mother.</i>

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:48.350
Besides, it's impossible!

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:50.850
Even if I make them apologize...

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:58.360
I don't think Chiho would ever
want to see their faces!

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:20.010
HINATA KAWAMOTO LOVES GUYS
PERVERTED GIRL
BITCH IDIOT

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:25.640
<i>There's one thing that I realized.</i>

00:20:38.990 --> 00:20:40.650
<i>I had thought...</i>

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:46.370
<i>...that if things got tough,
you can just get up and leave.</i>

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:48.870
3-2 KAWAMOTO

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:55.710
<i>When someone treats you improperly...</i>

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.590
<i>...you don't have to respond in a proper way.</i>

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:05.760
<i>But...</i>

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:14.020
Stand up!

00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:16.190
Bow!

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:19.030
HINATA KAWAMOTO LOVES GUYS
PERVERTED GIRL
BITCH IDIOT

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:22.030
Wh—

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:25.660
M-Ms. Kawamoto, what's the meaning of this?

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:33.540
I don't know.

00:21:34.120 --> 00:21:36.330
I'm not the one who wrote it.

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:47.890
Chiho Sakura: Absent/Absent/Absent

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:47.890
<i>I think you're misreading it, Ms. Kawamoto.</i>

00:21:48.350 --> 00:21:52.180
<i>You shouldn't turn
every situation into a bad one.</i>

00:21:55.810 --> 00:21:58.770
It was already written on the board
when I came in this morning.

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:15.210
A-Anyway, let's begin the lesson.

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:18.670
Ms. Kawamoto, please see me
in the faculty room after class.

00:22:25.300 --> 00:22:28.430
Come on, concentrate! Stop your whispering!

00:22:29.390 --> 00:22:31.180
Let's have a good game.

00:22:34.930 --> 00:22:36.520
<i>That's right.</i>

00:22:38.520 --> 00:22:40.480
<i>She's not only in pain.</i>

00:22:42.030 --> 00:22:43.530
<i>She's angry.</i>

00:22:44.780 --> 00:22:49.740
<i>In fact, she's seething
from the pit of her stomach.</i>

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:00.040
Letter

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:37.970
Episode 29

00:24:32.390 --> 00:24:34.050
No, don't look at me!

00:24:34.050 --> 00:24:36.010
Sis, get me a bath towel!

00:24:36.010 --> 00:24:39.100
What should we do?
It's terrible!

00:24:39.100 --> 00:24:42.020
Finally! We finally made it to this point!

00:24:42.150 --> 00:24:45.730
I'm the only one who can go
from our family.

00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:50.030
I bought peaches. Maybe I should've bought
ice cream instead.

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:58.500
ILLUSTRATION:
KOZUE AMANO

00:24:50.990 --> 00:24:54.200
Yoohoo, yoohoo, cherries!

00:24:54.570 --> 00:24:57.540
Derere, yummy magical fruit!
